  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "中小企業管理",
    "sub_ename": "SMALL BUSINESS MANAGEMENT",
    "describe_ch": "本課程在管理學的基礎上發展有關中小企業經營的相關知識，並從企業之創立與成長，探討小型企業在產、銷、人、發、財、各面向的特殊問題與管理成功之道，增進同學對於中小企業異於大企業之本質差異的認知，建立同學對家族企業、信用融通、市場利基定位、風險管理、創意創新創業等特定議題的熟悉度，並透過個案實務之分析，了解中小企業在產業中的重要性、限制性以及問題與機會，建立同學以掌握對於中小企業之管理問題解析能力。",
    "describe_eh": "This course in management studies based on the development of the SMEs management of knowledge, and the establishment and growth of enterprises, to explore the small businesses in the production, marketing, human resources, research and development, financial all aspects of the special problems and management success, to promote awareness of the students different from large enterprises to SMEs essential difference, to establish the degree of students' familiarity with the specific issues of family businesses, credit facilities, market niche positioning, risk management, creative innovation and entrepreneurship, through the practical analysis of the cases to understand the importance of SMEs in the industry, restrictive and problems and opportunities, to establish the students to solve the analytical ability to grasp the issue of management of small and medium enterprises.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 3.0
  },
  "targets": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "describe_ch": "能夠列舉中小企業的重要管理議題：分析各項議題的關鍵考量因素",
      "describe_en": "Be able to describe the specific issues for SME management; can evaluate the factors influencing the strategies for SMEs in front of these issues."
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "describe_ch": "能夠建立中小企業創業模式與企業成長途徑並分析其重要的影響因子",
      "describe_en": "Can construct the models of small business entrepreneur and growth; be able to analyze their critical success factors."
    },
    {
      "seq": 3,
      "describe_ch": "能夠比較並歸納中小企業實例個案之管理策略並在國際化背景中討論現代中小企業之行銷問題",
      "describe_en": "Be able to summarize the problems and opportunities of SMEs and discuss their internationalization from empirical cases."
    }
  ],
